# Elastic Plan values overscroll

Allow the scrolling values pane to reveal temporary white space beneath the fixed header when pulled down, then spring back into row alignment.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Pulling downward on plan values moves the value rows below their normal top position and reveals white space between them and the fixed header.
- [x] Releasing the pull springs values smoothly back to their aligned resting position.
- [x] The fixed plan-name pane, fixed column headers, and meta-header do not move during the pull.
- [x] The effect works in Default and Custom tables, including expanded custom rows.
- [x] Normal vertical scrolling and bottom-edge upward overscroll remain unchanged.
- [x] Horizontal summary/probability navigation remains synchronized and unaffected.
- [x] Offset normalization cannot leave fixed and value rows permanently misaligned.
- [x] Automated scroll-state coverage compiles.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This supersedes the earlier approach that counteracted all downward overscroll to keep values visually locked.

## Evidence

- Removed the values-pane counter-offset so native downward elasticity reveals the table background and springs back naturally.
- Negative elastic offsets normalize to zero before driving fixed-pane/header synchronization; positive vertical and horizontal scrolling remain unchanged.
- Added scroll-state coverage for downward elasticity, ordinary two-axis scrolling, and horizontal scrolling during a vertical pull.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing` compiled the app and both test bundles using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks025-030-derived`; live elastic-motion verification remains manual.
